From: Build compatibility fix
Subject: [PATCH] Use sd_bus_add_match for JobRemoved signals

sd_bus_match_signal is unavailable in the systemd headers used by this build.
Register the equivalent D-Bus signal match through the older sd_bus_add_match
API instead.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/systemd.c
+++ b/src/systemd.c
@@ -231,2 +231,5 @@
-	sdret = sd_bus_match_signal(bus, NULL, sender, path, interface,
-				    "JobRemoved", job_removed_callback, &job_path);
+	sdret = sd_bus_add_match(bus, NULL,
+				 "type='signal',sender='org.freedesktop.systemd1',"
+				 "path='/org/freedesktop/systemd1',"
+				 "interface='org.freedesktop.systemd1.Manager',member='JobRemoved'",
+				 job_removed_callback, &job_path);
